# LAW OWNERSHIP, from the law library (note/project/term/assurance/prove-loop/decision/002-law-library.md): after any
# sequence of events, every deleted note was deleted by its owner or an admin. The events are run from the empty state
# through the app's own `step` (`replay-events`, made here), so the law is about `step` itself and no replay of the
# app's can skip one.
#
# A project states the law by FUSING this template with its own forms and its step task, and proves the claim it
# makes with a `task ownership` of its own. It may not write the claim itself: `term knit` refuses a claim named
# `ownership` that is not this one (call/code/knit-law.ts). The template is used IN the file that fuses it: `term knit`
# appends this text below a marker at that file's end, because `term hold --report` and the Lean exporter read only a
# file's own templates.
#
#   fuse ownership-law
#     bind state, shelf
#     bind note, note
#     bind natural, natural
#     bind rank, rank
#     bind person, person
#     bind events, events
#     bind step, step
#
# THE SHAPE IT READS, whatever the forms are called: `state` is a list with the cases `bare` and `more` (`top`, a
# note, and `rest`), a note has the cases `live` (`at`, `whose`) and `gone` (`at`, `whose`, `by`, the person who
# deleted it), `person` is a record of `id` (a `natural`) and `rank`, whose case `admin` is the admin, `events` is a
# list with the cases `begin` and `after` (`event`, the latest, and `earlier`), and `step` takes the state and an event
# to the next state.
#
# Its shape is law.tree's `ownership-of-replay` in test/assurance/notes, the notes demo, with `allowed`, `fair` and
# `fair-shelf` from the same file. The body is written so it reads the same in a lean file and a longhand one.

tree ownership-law
  take state, like name
  take note, like name
  take natural, like name
  take rank, like name
  take person, like name
  take events, like name
  take step, like name

  hook fuse
    # THE POLICY: a person may delete a note when the person is an admin, or owns it
    form allowed
      head by, like {person}
      head whose, like {natural}
      case as-admin
        link i, like {natural}
        link w, like {natural}
        head
          make {person}
            bind id, i
            bind rank, make admin
        head
          read w
      case as-owner
        link w, like {natural}
        link r, like {rank}
        head
          make {person}
            bind id, w
            bind rank, r
        head
          read w

    # A FAIR note: live, or deleted by someone the policy allowed
    form fair
      head n, like {note}
      case fresh
        link at, like {natural}
        link whose, like {natural}
        head
          make live
            bind at, at
            bind whose, whose
      case buried
        link at, like {natural}
        link whose, like {natural}
        link by, like {person}
        link allowed-by
          like allowed
            head
              read by
            head
              read whose
        head
          make gone
            bind at, at
            bind whose, whose
            bind by, by

    # every note on the list is fair
    form fair-shelf
      head s, like {state}
      case clean
        head
          make bare
      case also
        link top, like {note}
        link rest, like {state}
        link top-fair
          like fair
            head
              read top
        link rest-fair
          like fair-shelf
            head
              read rest
        head
          make more
            bind top, top
            bind rest, rest

    # the events, run through `step` from the empty state
    task replay-events
      take es, like {events}
      like {state}
      sift es
        case begin
          send back, make bare
        case after
          send back
            call {step}
              call replay-events
                read earlier
              read event

    # OWNERSHIP: after any events, every note `step` has deleted was deleted by its owner or an admin
    rule ownership
      take es, like {events}
      like fair-shelf
        head
          call replay-events
            read es
